      "title": "Gold Opens Up 250 Baht, Ornaments Reach 72,900 Baht",
      "brief_text": "Domestic gold prices opened today (Aug. 26) up 250 baht per baht-weight, with gold ornaments selling at 72,900.00 baht and gold bars at 72,100.00 baht. Meanwhile, Gold Spot stood at 4,657.00 dollars per ounce. Global gold prices remain near their highest level in over three months, supported by a weaker dollar and the U.S. Treasury's bond buyback plan. Investors are also watching remarks by Kevin Warsh, Chairman of the U.S. Federal Reserve, at the Jackson Hole Symposium, which could influence interest rate direction and gold prices.",
