 "answer_to_user": "Gold (the metal) — GOLD.COMM last ~$4,716/oz. It's in a strong uptrend (above both its 50- and 200-day averages), +8.0% over the past week, +16.8% over the past month and +39.2% over the past year (upper half of its 52-week range, ~15.6% off the peak). So yes, it's ripping.\n\nThe MINERS are giving you leveraged beta to it — they've outrun the metal:\n• Newmont (NEM.US, ~$142bn) — +48% 1mo / +89% 1y\n• Agnico Eagle (AEM.US, ~$114bn) — +56% 1mo / +62% 1y\n• Barrick (B.US, ~$80bn) — +33% 1mo / +87% 1y\n• Kinross (KGC.US, ~$40bn) — +43% 1mo / +66% 1y\n• Wheaton Precious Metals (WPM.US, ~$74bn, streamer) — +50% 1mo / +70% 1y\n\nOther large names in the cohort: Franco-Nevada (FNV.US, royalty, ~$52bn), Royal Gold (RGLD.US), Alamos (AGI.US), IAMGold (IAG.US), Eldorado (EGO.US), B2Gold (BTG.US).\n\nRead: the metal is up ~39% over the year but the leading miners are up 60-90% — classic operating-leverage kicker (their margins expand faster than the gold price). Metal ≈ steady trend; miners = higher-beta expression of the same move. Note the miner-heavy names are largely Canada-domiciled, shown here on their US listings."
